    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "# FINAL NOTEBOOK RESULTS\n",
    "\n",
    "## What We Did\n",
    "Trained and evaluated multiple ML models on a synthetic target variable.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Results\n",
    "1. Determined that no legitimate labels exist for supervised ML\n",
    "2. Created a synthetic target for demonstration purposes\n",
    "3. Trained Random Forest, Logistic Regression, and Naive Bayes models\n",
    "4. Evaluated models using accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score\n",
    "\n",
    "## Result Interpretation\n",
    "The ML models can predict the synthetic target, but this is not a legitimate ML setup. The project should rely on rule-based matching rather than supervised ML.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Data Science Decisions\n",
    "- Do NOT use supervised ML without legitimate labels\n",
    "- Use rule-based matching as the primary approach\n",
    "- Document the ML process for academic completeness\n",
    "\n",
    "## Outputs Produced\n",
    "- Model comparison: outputs/model_comparison.csv\n",
    "- Trained model: models/random_forest_model.pkl (demonstration only)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Limitations\n",
    "- No legitimate labels for supervised learning\n",
    "- Synthetic target creates data leakage\n",
    "- Results are not meaningful for real predictions\n",
    "\n",
    "## Connection to the Next Notebook\n",
    "Notebook 11 will calculate career readiness scores using the rule-based matching results."
